  "Pipeline-health/digest aggregates that sound related can read disjoint tables or predicates (e.g. openHandoffs reads deploy_handoffs.status while paidNotLive reads leads.stage — a lead promoted without a handoff row is invisible to the former). Before assuming a new aggregate is already covered by a sibling, check what table/predicate it actually reads. Every fulfillment/money due-queue on the summary-card grid carries an 'oldest Xh' staleness signal on both dashboard and digest; for a calendar-cadence queue (month/week-keyed), anchor age to the later of the cadence boundary and the record's createdAt, never raw tenure alone, or a long-lived subscriber's queue looks perpetually fresh every reset.",
